# Comfy Registry publish

GitHub Release / tag / `CHANGELOG.md` alone do **not** fill the registry **Updates** section.

`comfy node publish` does **not** auto-read `CHANGELOG.md` or former `RELEASE_NOTES_*.md` files. Updates appear only when changelog text is passed explicitly:

```powershell
comfy node publish --changelog-file notes-<version>.md
# or: --changelog "..."  /  env COMFY_NODE_CHANGELOG
```

Release checklist:

1. Bump `pyproject.toml` `[project].version`
2. Move `CHANGELOG.md` `## Unreleased` into `## x.y.z — YYYY-MM-DD`
3. Commit, tag `x.y.z`, push, `gh release create` (GitHub notes optional)
4. Publish to registry **with** `--changelog` / `--changelog-file` (excerpt for that version only)
5. Confirm Updates on https://registry.comfy.org/publishers/kaze/nodes/sd-comfyui-style-organizer

If a version was published without changelog: delete that version on the registry UI, then republish with the flag.
